{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D25ufqNFG3f1667W4CwCZ6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"reddit menopause \"weight gain\" \"belly\" \"hot flashes\" \"night sweats\" \"brain fog\" what helped perimenopause experiences\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"menopause symptoms\",\"url\":\"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/blog/menopause-symptoms\"},{\"title\":\"menopause symptoms\",\"url\":\"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/blog/health/menopause-symptoms\"},{\"title\":\"Perimenopause & weight loss\",\"url\":\"https://community.myfitnesspal.com/en/discussion/comment/48202350\"},{\"title\":\"Women in Menopause tips and support for these changing times\",\"url\":\"https://community.myfitnesspal.com/en/discussion/comment/46987789\"},{\"title\":\"Women in Menopause tips and support for these changing times\",\"url\":\"https://community.myfitnesspal.com/en/discussion/comment/46990175\"},{\"title\":\"Women in Menopause tips and support for these changing times\",\"url\":\"https://community.myfitnesspal.com/en/discussion/comment/46993971\"},{\"title\":\"Menopause symptoms that may surprise you: What to watch for during perimenopause\",\"url\":\"https://www.health.harvard.edu/womens-health/menopause-symptoms-that-may-surprise-you-what-to-watch-for-during-perimenopause\"},{\"title\":\"www.weightwatchers.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/blog/weight-loss/perimenopause\"},{\"title\":\"www.weightwatchers.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/blog/perimenopause\"},{\"title\":\"www.weightwatchers.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/blog/health/perimenopause\"},{\"title\":\"Accessibility Statement\",\"url\":\"https://zoe.com/learn/perimenopause-weight-gain\"},{\"title\":\"Peri-Post Menopausal Weight Gain - What's Happening and What to Do About It\",\"url\":\"https://opentowellness.squarespace.com/blog/2020/3/6/menopause-weight-gain\"},{\"title\":\"Joyful Menopause\",\"url\":\"https://www.buzzsprout.com/2411915/episodes/17520746\"},{\"title\":\"top 12 symptoms menopause\",\"url\":\"https://www.weightwatchers.com/ca/en/blog/top-12-symptoms-menopause\"},{\"title\":\"Perimenopause and menopause symptoms and treatment options\",\"url\":\"https://healthy.kaiserpermanente.org/health-wellness/healtharticle.perimenopause-menopause-symptoms-and-treatment\"},{\"title\":\"Perimenopause Symptoms\",\"url\":\"https://www.swistle.com/2024/06/19/perimenopause-symptoms/\"},{\"title\":\"Joyful Menopause\",\"url\":\"https://www.buzzsprout.com/2411915/episodes/17354650-what-s-really-behind-your-menopause-symptoms-from-brain-fog-to-weight-gain-and-5-natural-fixes\"},{\"title\":\"4 signs of perimenopause that may affect your weight\",\"url\":\"https://blog.myfitnesspal.com/4-signs-of-perimenopause-that-may-affect-your-weight/\"},{\"title\":\"Aug 8, 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.joinmidi.com/post/meno-belly\"}]\n\nI ran one search, and it didn't return many Reddit threads. Most hits were forum posts from MyFitnessPal, plus health sites, so the anecdotes below are from those posts, not Reddit.\n\n**What people in those threads said helped:**\n- **Hormone therapy:** One poster said HRT helped a lot, and their hot flashes went away. Another said their insurer stopped covering it, so they tried going without it. Someone else reported they no longer drink and rarely get night sweats.\n- **An antidepressant:** One poster said an antidepressant helped both with mood and night sweats/insomnia.\n- **Alcohol:** Commenters linked drinking to worse night sweats, and one poster said extra alcohol hurt their weight.\n\n**Medical sources:**\n- For night sweats, Harvard Health says loose-fitting cotton PJs and lightweight bedding can help. It also notes that paroxetine (Brisdelle) and fezolinetant (Veozah) are FDA-approved to treat severe hot flashes and night sweats caused by menopause.\n- Kaiser Permanente says systemic hormone therapy is proven to help with hot flashes and night sweats, vaginal and bladder issues, and bone loss. It doesn't help with weight gain or mood changes.\n- For exercise, ZOE says a mix of aerobic and strength-based exercise can help with perimenopause symptoms like hot flashes and night sweats.\n- For belly fat, Midi Health describes a redistribution of weight that gives you that menopause belly. ZOE suggests that good nutrition, physical activity, and sleep may help prevent excess weight gain during perimenopause.\n- On brain fog, Harvard notes that frequently losing your train of thought and word-finding trouble are all symptoms of brain fog, which is common during perimenopause.\n\nForum experiences vary widely, and the medical sources are more reliable for treatment decisions. Anyone considering hormone therapy or a prescription should talk to a clinician, since the sources note HRT isn't recommended for everyone, such as people with a history of breast cancer, heart disease, or stroke.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62f71c28-0593-4b58-9060-c4b9304e6eb2","uuid":"c7304e5c-4af3-40c3-b846-8a03685debb7","timestamp":"2026-11-20T01:57:59.465Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"reddit menopause \"weight gain\" \"belly\" \"hot flashes\" \"night sweats\" \"brain fog\" what helped perimenopause experiences","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018GLe7fgE7M9YLcExnt443f","content":[{"title":"menopause symptoms","url":"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/blog/menopause-symptoms"},{"title":"menopause symptoms","url":"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/blog/health/menopause-symptoms"},{"title":"Perimenopause & weight loss","url":"https://community.myfitnesspal.com/en/discussion/comment/48202350"},{"title":"Women in Menopause tips and support for these changing times","url":"https://community.myfitnesspal.com/en/discussion/comment/46987789"},{"title":"Women in Menopause tips and support for these changing times","url":"https://community.myfitnesspal.com/en/discussion/comment/46990175"},{"title":"Women in Menopause tips and support for these changing times","url":"https://community.myfitnesspal.com/en/discussion/comment/46993971"},{"title":"Menopause symptoms that may surprise you: What to watch for during perimenopause","url":"https://www.health.harvard.edu/womens-health/menopause-symptoms-that-may-surprise-you-what-to-watch-for-during-perimenopause"},{"title":"www.weightwatchers.com","url":"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/blog/weight-loss/perimenopause"},{"title":"www.weightwatchers.com","url":"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/blog/perimenopause"},{"title":"www.weightwatchers.com","url":"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/blog/health/perimenopause"},{"title":"Accessibility Statement","url":"https://zoe.com/learn/perimenopause-weight-gain"},{"title":"Peri-Post Menopausal Weight Gain - What's Happening and What to Do About It","url":"https://opentowellness.squarespace.com/blog/2020/3/6/menopause-weight-gain"},{"title":"Joyful Menopause","url":"https://www.buzzsprout.com/2411915/episodes/17520746"},{"title":"top 12 symptoms menopause","url":"https://www.weightwatchers.com/ca/en/blog/top-12-symptoms-menopause"},{"title":"Perimenopause and menopause symptoms and treatment options","url":"https://healthy.kaiserpermanente.org/health-wellness/healtharticle.perimenopause-menopause-symptoms-and-treatment"},{"title":"Perimenopause Symptoms","url":"https://www.swistle.com/2024/06/19/perimenopause-symptoms/"},{"title":"Joyful Menopause","url":"https://www.buzzsprout.com/2411915/episodes/17354650-what-s-really-behind-your-menopause-symptoms-from-brain-fog-to-weight-gain-and-5-natural-fixes"},{"title":"4 signs of perimenopause that may affect your weight","url":"https://blog.myfitnesspal.com/4-signs-of-perimenopause-that-may-affect-your-weight/"},{"title":"Aug 8, 2024","url":"https://www.joinmidi.com/post/meno-belly"}]},"I ran one search, and it didn't return many Reddit threads. Most hits were forum posts from MyFitnessPal, plus health sites, so the anecdotes below are from those posts, not Reddit.\n\n**What people in those threads said helped:**\n- **Hormone therapy:** One poster said HRT helped a lot, and their hot flashes went away. Another said their insurer stopped covering it, so they tried going without it. Someone else reported they no longer drink and rarely get night sweats.\n- **An antidepressant:** One poster said an antidepressant helped both with mood and night sweats/insomnia.\n- **Alcohol:** Commenters linked drinking to worse night sweats, and one poster said extra alcohol hurt their weight.\n\n**Medical sources:**\n- For night sweats, Harvard Health says loose-fitting cotton PJs and lightweight bedding can help. It also notes that paroxetine (Brisdelle) and fezolinetant (Veozah) are FDA-approved to treat severe hot flashes and night sweats caused by menopause.\n- Kaiser Permanente says systemic hormone therapy is proven to help with hot flashes and night sweats, vaginal and bladder issues, and bone loss. It doesn't help with weight gain or mood changes.\n- For exercise, ZOE says a mix of aerobic and strength-based exercise can help with perimenopause symptoms like hot flashes and night sweats.\n- For belly fat, Midi Health describes a redistribution of weight that gives you that menopause belly. ZOE suggests that good nutrition, physical activity, and sleep may help prevent excess weight gain during perimenopause.\n- On brain fog, Harvard notes that frequently losing your train of thought and word-finding trouble are all symptoms of brain fog, which is common during perimenopause.\n\nForum experiences vary widely, and the medical sources are more reliable for treatment decisions. Anyone considering hormone therapy or a prescription should talk to a clinician, since the sources note HRT isn't recommended for everyone, such as people with a history of breast cancer, heart disease, or stroke."],"durationSeconds":5.847434582999995,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01D25ufqNFG3f1667W4CwCZ6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L51tQAQqwqEfdx7CBZePdu","type":"tool_result","content":"**Producto:** Isoflavones de Soya Tarro x 400 g (Isoretard, Tarro x 400 g), vendido por DEFARMA en Farmatodo.\n\n**Precio:** $69.900 (COP). La página indica 0 unidades disponibles y que el producto no está disponible actualmente.\n\n**Descripción:** Un \"Alimento funcional en polvo\" que combina macronutrientes, adaptógenos, fitoestrógenos y micronutrientes. Según la página, está pensado para los cambios hormonales, metabólicos y óseos de la perimenopausia y la menopausia.\n\n**Ingredientes:**\n- Proteína de quinoa, avena en polvo, colágeno hidrolizado, FOS (fructooligosacáridos) y maca en polvo\n- Ñame en polvo, isoflavones de soya, omega 3 y bromelina (enzima)\n- Minerales: potasio, gluconato de calcio, citrato de magnesio y cobre\n- Vitaminas: A, C, E, B1, B2, B3, B5, B6, B9 (ácido fólico) y B12\n\n**Porción:** 20 g en 200 mL de agua. Se agita o licúa y se consume recién preparado.\n\n**¿Es una bebida en polvo de soya?** La página no lo clasifica como bebida. Se describe como alimento funcional en polvo, pero se prepara con agua para consumirse como bebida. Su ingrediente principal de soya son los isoflavones, no una proteína de soya. Tampoco menciona que el producto sea una bebida de soya como tal.\n\n**Nota:** La página indica que se requiere cargar una fórmula médica para pedir este producto."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62f71c28-0593-4b58-9060-c4b9304e6eb2","uuid":"b4928cd6-de2d-4c94-8859-857d1a52dcbb","timestamp":"2026-11-20T01:58:01.475Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":324247,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Producto:** Isoflavones de Soya Tarro x 400 g (Isoretard, Tarro x 400 g), vendido por DEFARMA en Farmatodo.\n\n**Precio:** $69.900 (COP). La página indica 0 unidades disponibles y que el producto no está disponible actualmente.\n\n**Descripción:** Un \"Alimento funcional en polvo\" que combina macronutriente